, "titleIcon": "", "upPicture": "", "upperImage": "", "downPicture": "", "proprietaryTag": "", "buttonBackColor": "", "facilityShowStyle": 2, "isShieldAfterNameTag": true, "roomAtmosphereFacilityInfos": []}, "calendarRoomPackageInfo": {"pkId": 73285297, "pkType": 1, "showImg": [], "xProTitle": "Also included", "xProducts": [{"name": "Experiences & more", "title": "Vietnam 4G eSIM-QR code-3 days-Daily - 5GB (1)", "xType": 3, "itemInfo": [{"xUnit": "1", "xProID": 73272659, "element": [{"key": "Quantity\uff1a", "type": "0", "value": "1 serving per room", "isFold": false, "contents": []}, {"key": "Each suitable for\uff1a", "type": "2", "value": "1 guest", "isFold": false, "contents": []}, {"key": "Validity period\uff1a", "type": "9", "value": "Valid for 90 days from the booking date Valid for 1 use(s) only", "isFold": false, "contents": []}, {"key": "Exclusions\uff1a", "type": "14", "value": "", "isFold": false, "contents": ["Phone calls and text messages"]}, {"key": "Additional info\uff1a", "type": "7", "value": "Other notices\nInstructions for use\r\nHow to activate\r\n[Installing eSIM]  \n1. Open the QR code attachment in your Trip.com app order and print it in advance or save it to another electronic device. (For iOS 17 and above or certain Android phones, you can save the QR code image directly to your phone.)  \n2. Open Settings > Cellular (iOS) or SIM Card Management (Android).  \n3. With your phone connected to the internet, tap \"Add cellular plan\" (iOS) or \"Add mobile plan\" (Android), then scan the QR code to install.  \n4. If scanning fails, manually enter the \"SM-DP + Address\" and \"Activation Code\" from your order voucher to install.  \n5. If step 3 or 4 is unsuccessful, your phone may be carrier-locked (unable to use other carriers'' network bands). Contact your carrier to unlock it before using eSIM.  \n\n[Using eSIM]  \n1. Turn off your primary SIM and enable the eSIM network.  \n2. Enable Cellular (iOS) or SIM (Android).  \n3. Turn on data roaming.  \n4. If you still can''t connect after these steps, configure the APN and restart your phone (see details below).  \n\n[About APN]  \n1. If you purchased a multi-country/region eSIM and can''t connect upon arrival in a new area, manually switch the APN (normally it auto-switches).  \n2. Path: Cellular > Cellular Data Network, or Mobile Network > Mobile Data Network, or Mobile Services > Mobile Data Network.  \n3. Enter APN: mobile.three.com.hk  \n4. Restart your phone.\neSIM usage terms1. Device supports eSIM functionalityTo check: Open your phone''s dial pad and enter *#06#. If an EID is displayed, your device supports eSIM. If no EID appears, your device does not support eSIM.Unlocked mobile phoneCheck with your carrier to confirm if your device is network-locked. Please verify all the above conditions are met before purchase to ensure proper eSIM functionality.\nSet up eSIMPlease install and activate with an Internet connection after arriving at your destination. Installing in a non-destination country/region may cause the eSIM to become invalid or start counting usage time prematurely.If you encounter any installation issues, please carefully review the usage instructions section.\nEnable data roamingPlease ensure the \"Data Roaming\" option for your eSIM is enabled.\nNetwork instructionsSignal quality may vary depending on location, terrain, building obstructions, number of users, and weather conditions, which can affect Internet performance. Actual connectivity depends on local carrier coverage. When 5G is unavailable, your device will automatically switch to 4G/LTE signals.\nTrending sharesSupports hotspot sharing, but compatibility with all devices cannot be guaranteed due to model variations.\nDo not delete the eSIM after installation.A QR code can only be used on one mobile device. Once installed, it will be linked to that device and cannot be transferred to another.", "isFold": true, "contents": []}], "itemName": "Vietnam 4G eSIM-QR code-3 days-Daily - 5GB (1)", "imageList": ["https://ak-d.tripcdn.com/images/0350112000t4w8a2k6481_Mht8_3.jpg"], "menuInfos": [], "menuTitle": "Each package includes", "valueDesc": "", "xUnitDesc": "", "appointType": 0}]}], "specialInfo": ""}}}',NULL,NULL,1) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
